  "hints": [
    "the array is sorted - does a linear scan actually use that fact?",
    "if you check the middle element, what does that tell you about which half the target could be in?",
    "you can eliminate half the remaining elements with a single comparison - repeat that",
    "track left and right pointers, compute mid, compare arr[mid] to target, and move left or right accordingly"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "infinite loop from not updating left/right correctly (e.g. mid instead of mid+1/mid-1)",
    "integer overflow computing mid as (left+right)/2 in languages where this matters (mention left + (right-left)/2 as the safe form)",
    "off-by-one on the loop condition (left <= right vs left < right)"
  ],
